---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="About AISEOOnline — Evidence-first SEO utilities"
  description="Learn what AISEOOnline checks, how its open-source tools work, and which capabilities are still under development."
>
  <section class="page-banner">
    <div class="site-container max-w-4xl">
      <p class="eyebrow">About the project</p>
      <h1 class="section-title mt-4">Useful SEO checks. Evidence before assumptions.</h1>
      <p class="page-intro">
        AISEOOnline is an open-source collection of small website tools for developers, site owners
        and content teams. Each checker focuses on one question instead of inventing a sitewide SEO
        score.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section-space">
    <div class="site-container max-w-3xl space-y-7 leading-8 text-slate-700">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-950">What you can inspect</h2>
      <p>
        Ten tool interfaces are implemented: nine deterministic checks for robots files, XML
        sitemaps, metadata, redirects, canonical hints, JSON-LD, headings, internal links and social
        metadata, plus an optional AI title and description generator. Deterministic reports
        describe fetched evidence. The AI tool is separated from those findings and requires
        configured model service and human review.
      </p>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-950">How the project is built</h2>
      <p>
        The public interface uses Astro, React and TypeScript. FastAPI runs the bounded HTTP checks,
        while PostgreSQL, Redis and Celery support private development workflows. Limits and
        authentication protect more expensive features. Private deep auditing and private RAG
        assistants are not generally available in production.
      </p>
      <p>
        Source code, tests, methodology and limitations are published in the <a
          class="inline-link"
          href="https://github.com/bharathumashankar/aiseoonline">public GitHub repository</a
        > under Apache 2.0. See the <a class="inline-link" href="/open-source/benchmarks/"
          >evaluation methodology and recorded fixture results</a
        > rather than treating artificial numbers as real search performance.
      </p>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-950">Who operates the service?</h2>
      <p>
        The repository is maintained under the GitHub account <a
          class="inline-link"
          href="https://github.com/bharathumashankar">bharathumashankar</a
        >. The public service's legal operator name, jurisdiction, address and formal support
        channel require confirmation before production publication. We do not claim an incorporated
        company or staffed support team.
      </p>
      <p>
        Start with the <a class="inline-link" href="/tools/">public checker directory</a>, read the <a
          class="inline-link"
          href="/guides/">SEO guides</a
        >, or review the <a class="inline-link" href="/contact/">contact options</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
